# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We pledge to make participation in this project a respectful,
welcoming, and harassment-free experience for everyone.

## Our Standards

Examples of behavior that contribute to a positive environment include:

- Being respectful and professional
- Welcoming different viewpoints
- Accepting constructive criticism
- Focusing on what is best for the project

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination,
personal attacks, and inappropriate conduct.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing
the standards of acceptable behavior.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies within project spaces and whenever
an individual is representing the project or its community.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project
maintainers. Reports will be reviewed and addressed appropriately.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Maintainers will investigate reports fairly and may take actions
such as warnings, temporary restrictions, or removal from project
activities where necessary.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct was adapted for educational use from the
Contributor Covenant.
